W: 1 The radiant morn hath passed away,
W: and spent too soon her golden store;
W: the shadows of departing day
W: creep on once more.
W:
W: 2 Our life is but an autumn sun,
W: its glorious noon how quickly past!
W: Lead us, O Christ, thou living Way,
W: safe home at last.
W:
W: 3 O by thy soul-inspiring grace
W: uplift our hearts to realms on high;
W: help us to look to that bright place
W: beyond the sky.
W:
W: 4 Where light and life and joy and peace
W: in undivided empire reign,
W: and thronging angels never cease
W: their deathless strain
W:
W: 5 where saints are clothed in spotless white,
W: and evening shadows never fall,
W: where thou, eternal Light of light,
W: art Lord of all.
W:</miscellaneous-field>
